WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:16.100
Hi, welcome back to our online retreat 
called "The Wheel of Life."

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.820
I'd like to thank Stanley for translating.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.320
We've reached session 23.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:34.160
The name of this session is called 
"Three Things for Cutting a Tree."

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:44.440
And you see a picture of a very strong guy 
with an axe that he's going to cut the tree.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.280
Let's jump into the text.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:58.460
nyipa ni (GNYIS PA NI),
Which means "number two." 
So I went got you what point number two, which is

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:02.420
lam ji tabu shik gi korwa le dokpa
(LAM JI LTA BU ZHIG GIS 'KHOR BA LAS LDOG PA)--

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.340
What's the path were going to use to get out of the Wheel?

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.760
rang chak gi korway tsawa chupa la
(RANG CAG GIS 'KHOR BA'I RTZA BA GCOD PA LA)--

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:21.980
now if we want to--we have an idiom in English called "throw a monkey wrench into the machine."

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:29.700
It means take a tool and throw it into those wheels 
and then suddenly everything goes [breaking noises] 
and it stops.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:45.040
We had a similar thing when we were kids.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:53.400
If there's a kid we don't like--and all of us have bicycles,

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.760
then we will run next to his bicycle,

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.860
with a big fat stick.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.480
And then we'll push it into the bicycle wheel,

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:14.460
and then it goes [breaking sound] 
and the whole wheel breaks.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.940
How do we throw a stick into the bicycle wheel?

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:28.400
korway tsawa de kona nyi la mongpay marikpa
('KHOR BA'I RTZA BA DE KHO NA NYID LA RMONGS PA'I MA RIG PA)--

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.820
we have to go after link number one,

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:40.500
which is misunderstanding the way reality works.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.960
You guys have a pen? 
I have a pen.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:54.160
In Diamond Cutter Institute language--and you should go to a Diamond Cutter Institute program--

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:01.100
we say that the pen, it looks like the pen is coming from the pen.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.180
But actually the pen is coming from me.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:11.380
You've been alive in this world for many years,

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:21.340
and all that time you didn't realize 
these are seeds in your mind making pictures 
that are the things around you.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:34.580
This misunderstanding is called 
hlenkye nyi (LHAN SKYES NYID). hlenkye nyi 
means "you are born with it."

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:46.640
Bugs are born with it, whales are born with it, 
birds are born with it.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:57.700
We've been talking about the example of the woman who comes home and her husband yells at her.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:06.580
And she says "I didn't do anything, and he yelled at me."

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:13.320
She's having a misunderstanding about her immediate world and her immediate self.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.640
And that's the classic form of the first link.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:29.340
We are misunderstanding ourselves 
and our immediate world.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:39.360
And that's actually the place where we can stop the machine of the suffering life.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:50.100
And again, it doesn't mean you're going to die or something like that.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:57.100
It means you enter a perfect life 
and a body which cannot die.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:07.880
Some American guy--the Americans have the most funny ideas about Buddhism--

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:16.140
"Geshe-la, I don't want to stop the Wheel of Life."

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:24.920
Why? "Because I want to die." 
Why do you want to die?

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:34.100
"Even after fifty years I've got so many wrinkles. 
If I live for five thousand years, do you know 
how many wrinkles I'm going to have?

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.820
I'm going to look terrible!"

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.180
It's not like that, okay?

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:49.760
You don't have to kill yourself to get out of the Wheel.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:57.400
And it's not like you're going to live for a thousand years and you got a thousand years of wrinkles.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:08.840
You will enter a perfect body, 
perfect mind, perfect heart.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:13.380
And all of the people you love will be around you
in their perfect form also.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:22.440
That's what happens if you stop the Wheel.

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:30.480
And you have to reach into the Wheel and stop it 
at the exact correct place.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:39.640
If you can't cut that exact place,

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:45.680
nyenpo shen gyi nyonmongpa
(GNYEN PO GZHAN GYIS NYON MONGS PA)--

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:56.080
and you use some other kind of antidote--"antidote" here means some other spiritual method to become free.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:04.240
nyonmongpa re shik drip
(NYON MONGS PA RE ZHIG 'GRIB)--

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:12.280
you will affect some of your negative thoughts and the things connected with your negative thoughts.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:22.540
The verb here in the Tibetan is very interesting.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:26.980
drip kyang ten du mi-se
('GRIB KYANG GTAN DU MI ZAD)--

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:32.860
you will slow down those negative thoughts, 
but you won't stop them forever.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:45.660
Like, you get angry when you drive on the road.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:55.620
This is one of my problems. Today.  
Some guy was driving very dangerously.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:59.960
Yeah, I get like, "Why you do that?"

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:05.720
So then maybe if Veronica is in the car,

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:13.760
she says, "Listen, you're a Buddhist teacher. 
You shouldn't get angry, even at the other driver."

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:24.700
And then I can be peaceful about the guy 
who drives dangerously next to me.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:37.960
But tomorrow if someone actually hits my car 
then my patience will break.

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:45.500
So normal patience has a limit.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:52.820
If someone push you, push you, push you, push you, push you... 
finally you will fight.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:09:02.040
That means you didn't find the real solution.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:13.520
So maybe most of you don't know how cement works.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:21.860
But my lama told me one day, 
"You make a sidewalk around the temple."

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:33.540
I said "I don't know anything about 
how to make a sidewalk." Then he looked at me 
like I'm crazy and said, "Well, just learn."

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:41.880
So I learned, and what's interesting about pouring cement...

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:50.220
You think like, "So how many days do we have to wait for the cement to get dry?"

00:09:52.840 --> 00:10:00.400
But that's not how cement works. 
When they arrive in the cement truck,

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:07.400
they mix together the water and the special chemical,

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:13.580
and it creates a chemical reaction.

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:21.200
The cement starts to react from the middle, from the inside

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:30.660
and it continues to get harder for thirty years.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:35.520
That reaction doesn't finish.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:41.320
To break old cement is almost impossible.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:53.900
It gets harder, and harder, and harder. 
And Buddhist path for patience

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:02.240
is different from a normal path for patience.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:12.900
In the normal path they say, 
"Kust try to be nice. Don't get angry."

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:22.300
But the sign that a solution is not perfect

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:30.980
is that if someone pushes you enough,

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:38.160
your patience will break.

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:43.940
Like, if they yell at you, you're like... "Ah, it's ok."

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:46.620
And they push you, and you're like... "Ah, it's ok."

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.800
And they hit you. "Ah, that's ok."

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:57.380
Then they hit your kid. Then you'll go crazy.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:01.780
That's the normal solution to anger.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:07.440
But the Buddhist solution to anger

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:17.320
is like cement, and every day it gets 
stronger, and stronger, and stronger.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:26.940
And the more you push that person,
the stronger they get.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:37.600
So we're talking about this kind of antidote. 
He says we don't want the solution which works 
for a while, but doesn't cure the disease.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:51.580
de na ngar dzin hlenkye le gewa shen gyi nu mi nupar
(DES NA NGAR 'DZIN LHAN SKYES LA DGE BA GZHAN GYIS GNOD MI NUS PAR)

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:57.100
We have this habit inside our mind.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:00.760
Bad things happen to us,

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:08.400
and, like the wife in the kitchen, 
we like to say, "I didn't do anything!

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:12.880
And now this thing is happening to me."

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:24.080
There's no kind of good karma 
which can stop that thinking.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:27.260
Except one.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:33.580
So when we talk about a path 
to get out of the Wheel of Life,

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:43.720
of course there are many different 
spiritual kinds of behaviour.

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:49.340
Be nice to people.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:51.850
Be compassionate.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.430
Do tong len (GTONG LEN).

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:56.780
Exchange self and others.

00:13:56.780 --> 00:14:02.240
Many, many. But they don't stop the root of the problem.

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:12.720
gewa shen gyi nu mi nupar
DGE BA GZHAN GYIS GNOD MI NUS PAR) means 
they don't hurt your "I didn't do anything" idea.

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:20.700
The only way to stop that idea, "I didn't do anything,"

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:29.060
is to find dzin tang ngu gal du song
('DZIN STANGS DNGOS 'GAL DU SONG).

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:36.000
dzin tang ('DZIN STANGS) means 
"the way it thinks about things"

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:47.140
should be the direct opposite--not just the opposite but the direct opposite-- of the way you are thinking.

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:57.330
So the dzin tang we're talking about in the kitchen,

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:01.060
the wife says, "I didn't do anything and he yelled at me."

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:11.600
Then the complete opposite of that idea, is "Oh, I did do something.

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:16.920
I yelled at my kids last week."

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:23.520
So in Buddhism, in the deepest forms of meditation,

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:29.300
we are talking about one state of mind,

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:36.320
and we have to find a state of mind 
which is the direct opposite.

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:42.440
Then it can stop the first state of mind forever.

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:53.460
What's the first state of mind? "I came in the kitchen and he yelled at me. I didn't do anything!"

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:59.020
Okay, what's the direct opposite thinking?

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:05.560
She walks in the kitchen, he starts calling her stupid,

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:10.180
a real Buddhist, they're like this...

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.340
They don't say, "I'm not stupid, you're stupid."

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:17.400
They're like this [looks around]

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:31.280
What's that lady doing? She's just thinking. 
"How did I plant these bad seeds? What did I do last week?"

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:37.440
Probably the husband is really angry, 
he's all red, he's yelling.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:44.700
And before she studied lam rim (LAM RIM),

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:48.960
she'd say, "You're stupid, not me!"

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:56.980
After studying lam rim--especially Wheel of Life online lam rim--

00:16:56.980 --> 00:16:58.940
He goes, "You're stupid!"

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:01.640
and she goes...

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:08.620
It means, "Oh, what did I do last week?"

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:13.780
Okay? That thinking, "What did I do last week?"

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:23.020
is the direct nuclear bomb which stops the first link.

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:31.180
de yang dakme tokpay sherab nyi kyi nga rangshin gyi mepar tokpe
(DE YANG BDAG MED RTOGS PA'I SHES RAB NYID KYIS NGA RANG BZHIN GYIS MED PAR RTOGS PAS)

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:39.960
Then the wisdom which understands 
"I am not the person I used to think I was,"

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:51.600
it understands these things are not happening to me in the kitchen for no reason at all.

00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:01.410
nga rangshin gyi druppar dzinpay lo dang dzin tang ngu su galwa yin pe
(NGA RANG BZHIN GYIS GRUB PAR 'DZIN PA'I BLO DANG 'DZIN STANGS DNGOS SU 'GAL BA YIN PAS)

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:08.920
We have to find a state of mind which is opposite of 
"I didn't do anything and he yelled at me."

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:16.520
We need a state of wisdom

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:24.640
which can put the monkey wrench into the middle of the machine and blow up the whole machine.

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:32.100
di me na ('DI MED NA)--if you don't have that,

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:35.980
gewa shen jindra shik la be kyang
(DGE BA GZHAN JI 'DRA ZHIG LA 'BAD KYANG)--

00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:44.200
You can work really, really hard to develop other 
good qualities, good spiritual qualities.

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:52.380
More patience.

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:54.320
More morality.

00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:56.240
More compassion.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:59.800
More joy for doing good things.

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:04.540
More general meditation.

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:11.220
And those will help your wisdom. 
They will support your wisdom.

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:22.600
No, I'm sorry I made a mistake. 
He said something worse than that. 
Okay, ready?

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:29.520
If all those spiritual practices

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:34.380
don't have wisdom in them,

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:42.340
they become a support for the wrong idea.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:58.960
Let's go back to the kitchen. She just came back from some place where they teach "just be patient."

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:11.080
She just came back from a place where they teach you to be patient about your husband,

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:16.980
but they don't teach you that the husband 
you're being patient with is coming from you.

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:40.840
So you go to some therapist and you say "I have trouble, I feel angry at my husband when he calls me stupid."

00:20:46.820 --> 00:20:52.480
Then the therapist says, "Well, next time you walk in the kitchen and he starts yelling at you,

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:02.600
just try to be a little more understanding.

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:06.120
Maybe he had a hard day.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:09.320
Maybe he has a headache.

00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:12.220
Maybe his boss yelled at him.

00:21:13.140 --> 00:21:16.260
Just try to calm down."

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:22.280
So try to imagine--that lady went to the therapist,

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:30.820
and she comes in the kitchen, 
and the husband says, "You're stupid."

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:33.900
She looks at him

00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:38.920
and she remembers her therapist.

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:43.680
"Oh, maybe he had a hard day.

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:48.140
Maybe he couldn't get lunch, maybe he's hungry.

00:21:50.140 --> 00:21:53.800
Maybe he had bad traffic on the way home today.

00:21:55.600 --> 00:22:00.460
I should try to just be patient with him.

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:04.740
It's possible something happened."

00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:09.640
In this section of the lam rim,

00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:14.500
they're saying something very radical.

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:24.320
Those two minutes trying to sympathize with your husband,

00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:31.240
which the therapist told you to do--

00:22:32.180 --> 00:22:33.860
listen,

00:22:33.860 --> 00:22:42.700
they actually make the feeling that he's not coming from you stronger for those two minutes.

00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:58.320
So for two minutes more, in your billions of lifetimes,

00:23:00.420 --> 00:23:08.420
you are looking at the pen or the husband, and you're having the feeling that he comes 'this way.'

00:23:12.860 --> 00:23:17.940
And in those two minutes of trying to be nice to him,

00:23:19.600 --> 00:23:24.160
but feeling that he's coming not from me,

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:32.680
will cause your suffering in the wheel of life to go on for more years.

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:40.100
Okay, it's a very radical statement.

00:23:41.120 --> 00:23:50.160
It means if in the middle of something frightening, or some anger, or something going on--

00:23:54.560 --> 00:24:02.980
like the virus. If you just think for two minutes, 
"Maybe this is coming from something I did,"

00:24:08.500 --> 00:24:14.040
then you are putting a monkey wrench in the middle of the machine and it will stop.

00:24:18.960 --> 00:24:21.900
sherab de gyu la lekpar kyepar jepa la
(SHES RAB DE RGYUD LA LEGS PAR BSKYED PAR BYED PA LA)

00:24:22.040 --> 00:24:32.060
And if you want to just keep increasing 
this awareness, when you walk in the kitchen remembering he's coming from you

00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:41.820
hlakpa ting ngendzin gyi lappa ma kyepar mi jung te
(LHAG PA TING NGE 'DZIN GYI BSLAB PA MA SKYES PAR MI 'BYUNG STE)--

00:24:41.820 --> 00:24:46.000
unless you meditate, it's not going to be strong enough.

00:24:49.500 --> 00:24:54.000
So if you don't practice meditation regularly,

00:24:57.460 --> 00:24:59.860
your basic state of mind

00:25:00.780 --> 00:25:08.660
will not be strong enough to keep 
the correct idea going in the kitchen while he's yelling.

00:25:17.200 --> 00:25:22.000
Practicing meditation even just a half hour every day...

00:25:23.640 --> 00:25:28.000
by the way the key to meditation 
is to start with ten minutes,

00:25:30.460 --> 00:25:32.460
never start with more than that.

00:25:34.500 --> 00:25:41.020
Sit down for ten minutes and meditate, 
but every morning, and don't break.

00:25:42.600 --> 00:25:45.180
I have a timer here.

00:25:46.620 --> 00:25:57.280
Set the timer for ten minutes. Every Sunday increase it by one minute.

00:25:58.580 --> 00:26:04.140
Then within one year, you're meditating for an hour. 
It's perfect.

00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:14.700
But don't try to use emptiness in the kitchen 
unless you are meditating everyday.

00:26:22.020 --> 00:26:28.240
You will not have enough control over your mind 
to keep the correct idea.

00:26:33.500 --> 00:26:41.220
So throwing the wrench 
into the bad machine in the kitchen,

00:26:47.900 --> 00:26:51.880
stopping the Wheel at the correct place,
at link number one,

00:26:54.580 --> 00:27:03.500
it's not going to work if you don't have a strong and peaceful state of mind, always.

00:27:07.500 --> 00:27:12.260
It has to go together with meditation.

00:27:13.400 --> 00:27:18.700
Now Pabongka Rinpoche goes into a famous metaphor.

00:27:22.900 --> 00:27:28.480
And I remember when I first heard it forty years ago.

00:27:31.300 --> 00:27:35.440
It's the kind of metaphor that stays with you.

00:27:38.140 --> 00:27:43.240
I think I heard it in the first month 
I was studying Buddhism.

00:27:45.100 --> 00:27:47.380
He says, per na shing gi dongpo chupa la
(DPER NA SHING GI SDONG PO GCOD PA LA)

00:27:47.380 --> 00:27:52.180
Let's say you want to cut down a big tree.

00:27:57.140 --> 00:28:06.760
You're going to need some different things. Number one, 
ta re nunpo (STA RE RNON PO) means you're going to need a very sharp axe.

00:28:11.640 --> 00:28:17.040
And you're going to need two big pungpa (DPUNG PA).

00:28:17.920 --> 00:28:20.200
So, what's a punpa?

00:28:20.620 --> 00:28:22.519
What's a pungpa? pungpa means--

00:28:22.520 --> 00:28:31.900
your arm from the elbow up to the top of the shoulder, and we don't have a separate word in English.

00:28:35.660 --> 00:28:39.400
You can say strong shoulder, but that's this part.

00:28:40.700 --> 00:28:44.000
You could say strong bicep, but that's only this part.

00:28:45.960 --> 00:28:49.320
But this Tibetan word covers both.

00:28:51.680 --> 00:28:55.640
It says "you need two good pungpas."

00:28:58.160 --> 00:29:04.240
So now you need two things. You need a sharp axe,

00:29:05.880 --> 00:29:13.340
and you need to be buff--you need to be strong here. 
And we have that picture right?

00:29:16.460 --> 00:29:21.180
de yang ta re nunpo me na
(DE YANG STA RE RNON PO MED NA)--
if you don't have a sharp axe,

00:29:22.780 --> 00:29:28.800
shing dong chu mi nu
(SHING SDONG GCOD MI NUS)--
there's no way you're going to cut the tree.

00:29:29.960 --> 00:29:35.540
If you don't have the right tool, 
you can't do even a basic thing. 
We learned that the other night.

00:29:39.500 --> 00:29:44.060
We didn't have the right tool and we spent half an hour.

00:29:47.360 --> 00:29:56.440
pungpa tenpo me na (DPUNG PA BRTAN PO MED NA)--
and if you don't have strong sturdy shoulders 
and upper arms,

00:29:58.100 --> 00:30:00.100
ta re ne chik tu mi bap
(STA RE GNAS GCIG TU MI 'BAB)

00:30:00.440 --> 00:30:10.520
you won't be able to control where the axe hits on the tree, because when you cut wood you have to cut a specific pattern.

00:30:19.540 --> 00:30:28.780
Then he kind of gives a related example to this kind of focusing the axe on the right place.

00:30:33.940 --> 00:30:37.020
Let's say tsen mor (MTSAN MOR)--
it's "night time."

00:30:38.460 --> 00:30:43.900
gyang ri tawa (GYANG RIS BLTA BA)--
you want to "look at something that's pretty far away."

00:30:46.800 --> 00:30:51.260
You need a nice strong candle,

00:30:54.100 --> 00:30:58.440
and the wind shouldn't be blowing the candle.

00:31:01.560 --> 00:31:04.340
So there has to be some steady focus.

00:31:06.700 --> 00:31:12.380
Sharp axe. Steady focus. Stong arms.

00:31:12.860 --> 00:31:16.960
dakme tokpay sherab ta re nunpo
(BDAG MED RTOGS PA'I SHES RAB STA RE RNON PO)

00:31:17.100 --> 00:31:22.140
What is your sharp axe in this case?

00:31:25.980 --> 00:31:35.660
It's the moment in the kitchen when the wife says, 
"Oh, I yelled at the kid last week.

00:31:42.380 --> 00:31:49.860
There doesn't even exist a husband in the kitchen who doesn't come directly from me."

00:31:53.740 --> 00:32:03.280
So that's like a sharp axe--
her thought in the kitchen that "he's coming from me."

00:32:05.380 --> 00:32:13.060
That's like a sharp axe. Or you can say she has a very steady candle.

00:32:14.500 --> 00:32:17.120
den dzin gyi shing gi dongpo chu
(BDEN 'DZIN GYI SHING GI SDONG PO GCOD)

00:32:17.120 --> 00:32:25.740
Then you can cut down that belief in fake reality.

00:32:33.300 --> 00:32:35.300
What's a fake reality?

00:32:35.880 --> 00:32:37.400
"I didn't do anything and he yelled at me!"

00:32:37.720 --> 00:32:43.420
So don't get all philosophical with these Buddhist ideas.

00:32:46.980 --> 00:32:52.860
There are millions and millions of people who have lived in this world and never heard these ideas.

00:32:57.000 --> 00:33:06.060
Then there are hundreds and hundreds of people who heard them, but studied them their whole life and didn't understand what the wife already understood.

00:33:13.720 --> 00:33:23.240
...
She has the candle now. And it's not shaking.

00:33:24.660 --> 00:33:27.220
Then she can cut the tree.

00:33:27.560 --> 00:33:29.480
What's the tree?

00:33:31.760 --> 00:33:33.760
[Stanley, "I didn't do anything."]
Yeah, good.

00:33:34.380 --> 00:33:40.320
Very easy. 
"No Geshe-la, it's too easy.
The scriptures are very deep."

00:33:44.800 --> 00:33:51.180
If you can use the emptiness in the kitchen, 
you went deeper than any sutra, okay?

00:33:56.760 --> 00:34:01.340
ne luk ji shin tongwa la ni ta re dzin je kyi pungpa tenpo
(GNAS LUGS JI BZHIN MTHONG BA LA NI STA RE 'DZIN BYED KYI DPUNG PA BRTAN PO)

00:34:01.340 --> 00:34:11.500
So you need the strong arms of seeing 
what's really going on in the kitchen.

00:34:18.860 --> 00:34:25.740
And to go deeply into the emptiness of the husband you used to think was in the kitchen,

00:34:30.880 --> 00:34:38.100
you need a strong state of concentration, of focus, which can hold on to that idea, because every time,

00:34:38.440 --> 00:34:46.340
every minute that goes by in the kitchen and he keeps yelling at you, it's possible you will lose your focus.

00:34:55.700 --> 00:34:58.260
You need tse chikpay ting ngendzin tenpo
(RTZE GCIG PA'I TING NGE 'DZIN BRTAN PO)

00:34:58.260 --> 00:35:02.420
You need focus which is unshakeable.

00:35:05.020 --> 00:35:08.940
sems nang gi yengwa dang drelway ting ngendzin tenpo gyu la kyewa la-ang
(SEMS NANG GI G-YENG BA DANG BRAL BA'I TING NGE 'DZIN BRTAN PO RGYUD LA SKYE BA LA'ANG)

00:35:08.940 --> 00:35:12.080
But even if you have this strong focus,

00:35:13.640 --> 00:35:19.360
sem chi rol gyi yengwa rakpa dang drel je hlakpa tsultrim kyi lappa kye gu
(SEMS PHYI ROL GYI G-YENG BA RAGS PA DANG BRAL BYED LHAG PA TSUL KHRIMS KYI 
BSLAB PA SKYE DGOS)

00:35:19.560 --> 00:35:28.360
A peaceful state of mind comes from living a general peaceful life all day long.

00:35:33.700 --> 00:35:38.800
You cannot live a life which is not pure,

00:35:44.820 --> 00:35:50.340
and then suddenly in the kitchen, you're going to remember that he's coming from you.

00:35:51.800 --> 00:35:53.800
It's not going to happen.

00:35:54.960 --> 00:36:00.300
Not just your morning meditation.
That's not the only support you need.

00:36:04.200 --> 00:36:10.140
You need the support 
of a whole day-long pure way of life

00:36:17.260 --> 00:36:21.300
where you are being kind to other people.

00:36:23.120 --> 00:36:27.540
Which we call "the ethical life."

00:36:29.120 --> 00:36:36.780
It's... in Buddhism it's called "the extraordinary practice of the ethical way of life."

00:36:41.320 --> 00:36:44.240
It doesn't matter how good your focus is.

00:36:47.840 --> 00:36:57.640
That focus will waver in the kitchen.
If he yells at you for five, ten, twenty minutes--

00:36:58.720 --> 00:37:00.720
you will lose the focus.

00:37:01.620 --> 00:37:05.780
You will lose the understanding 
that it came from yelling at your kids,

00:37:10.960 --> 00:37:21.560
unless your mind is already 
in the big comfortable bed called "all-day morality."

00:37:28.940 --> 00:37:32.940
dor na, tsangpe shupa say ngu shir drangpa le
(MDOR NA, TSANGS PAS ZHUS PA SA'I DNGOS GZHIR DRANGS PA LAS,)

00:37:32.940 --> 00:37:43.640
He quotes a quotation found in a famous book by Asanga called "The Foundation of the Levels."

00:37:48.780 --> 00:37:57.220
It's a sutra called the 
"Sutra Requested by the Deva Bahma."

00:38:00.480 --> 00:38:03.954
tsawa shintu tenpa dang, shiway sems la gawa dang, pakpay ta dang dikpay ta, denpar ja shing drelwar ja

00:38:03.954 --> 00:38:08.540
(,RTZA BA SHIN TU BRTAN PA DANG,
,ZHI BA'I SEMS LA DGA' BA DANG,
,'PHAGS PA'I LTA DANG SDIG PA'I LTA,
,LDAN PAR BYA ZHING BRAL BAR BYA,)

00:38:09.300 --> 00:38:12.240
Your roots should be very strong.

00:38:21.660 --> 00:38:26.500
shiway sem la gawa (ZHI BA'I SEMS LA DGA' BA)--
you should enjoy a peaceful state of mind.

00:38:30.780 --> 00:38:33.100
There's two possibilities.

00:38:33.780 --> 00:38:41.360
You could have the viewpoint of an Arya, or you could have the viewpoint of a person who likes to hurt people.

00:38:49.240 --> 00:38:53.320
Embrace the first one and reject the second one.

00:38:55.160 --> 00:39:02.760
Think like an Arya, and reject this idea 
that it's okay to hurt other people.

00:39:04.860 --> 00:39:09.840
Then Pabongka Rinpoche says, "What's the sutra talking about?"

00:39:11.840 --> 00:39:15.760
dak dzin gyi nyenpo yangdakpay ne luk stong nyi tokpay pakpay tawa
(BDAG 'DZIN GYI GNYEN PO YANG DAG PA'I GNAS LUGS STONG NYID RTOGS PA'I 'PHAGS PA'I LTA BA)

00:39:15.760 --> 00:39:20.960
What do we mean "Arya's point of view?"

00:39:21.640 --> 00:39:28.580
That point of view remembers 
the emptiness in the kitchen.

00:39:33.980 --> 00:39:37.180
What's the emptiness in the kitchen?

00:39:37.740 --> 00:39:49.540
There is not now, and there was never in the past, 
and there will never be in the future,

00:39:50.160 --> 00:39:54.360
a husband who stands in my kitchen,

00:39:55.960 --> 00:39:59.260
who doesn't come from me, directly.

00:40:01.040 --> 00:40:03.380
Okay, that's emptiness.

00:40:03.780 --> 00:40:07.920
By the way, that's called hlak tong (LHAG MTHONG)--

00:40:08.540 --> 00:40:15.780
Vipashyana [Vipaśyanā].  
Okay. First of all, it's not pronounced "vipassana."

00:40:17.560 --> 00:40:21.120
That's a corruption of the word "vipashyana."

00:40:23.180 --> 00:40:26.660
And it doesn't refer to meditation.

00:40:27.680 --> 00:40:32.100
It refers to a special viewpoint.

00:40:33.080 --> 00:40:39.760
It even means "special viewpoint."
vi means "special" and pashyana means "viewpoint," "view."

00:40:42.200 --> 00:40:44.200
What is that?

00:40:44.600 --> 00:40:52.540
"I thought he was just yelling at me. But now I understand he's coming from me because I yelled at my kids.

00:40:55.900 --> 00:41:00.580
Right there, in the kitchen, he's coming from me.

00:41:01.340 --> 00:41:05.160
The husband I used to think was there was never there."

00:41:07.540 --> 00:41:10.540
What husband was never there?

00:41:11.900 --> 00:41:14.180
"I didn't do anything husband."

00:41:14.540 --> 00:41:20.300
But to hold that thought in your mind 
while your husband is yelling,

00:41:23.920 --> 00:41:28.500
you're going to need meditation.
You're going to need powerful meditation.

00:41:32.510 --> 00:41:41.080
And specifically the powerful meditation which can hold the idea in your mind that he's not coming from his side.

00:41:46.000 --> 00:41:53.580
That powerful state of meditation which holds on to that kind of emptiness is called shamatha [śamatha].

00:42:00.900 --> 00:42:05.240
shamatha means "a super peaceful state of mind."

00:42:07.820 --> 00:42:15.740
In this month-long course, we were exploring shamatha

00:42:17.400 --> 00:42:22.500
when we went through the eight 
form and formless realm meditations.

00:42:26.120 --> 00:42:32.680
Those meditations did not have a meaningful object.

00:42:35.120 --> 00:42:40.660
Like you cannot stop your mind, 
we just pretend to stop your mind.

00:42:43.100 --> 00:42:47.960
But if you work on those eight steps, which we did,

00:42:51.080 --> 00:43:01.760
your mind will become extremely peaceful like the surface of a lake at night when there's no wind at all.

00:43:09.520 --> 00:43:13.800
And the name of that 
peaceful state of mind is "shamatha."

00:43:18.420 --> 00:43:27.820
So it's beautiful to see a full moon reflected on the top of a lake at night with no ripples. Perfect.

00:43:39.060 --> 00:43:41.560
But it's not going to help you.

00:43:42.360 --> 00:43:48.480
You need to turn that 
peaceful state of mind on a high object.

00:43:52.860 --> 00:43:55.980
What's the high object in our case?

00:43:57.420 --> 00:44:01.020
"Oh, it looks like he's yelling from his side,

00:44:03.500 --> 00:44:05.500
but it's coming from me."

00:44:06.329 --> 00:44:12.469
So we got this. Now we have a correct idea 
about where the husband's yelling comes from.

00:44:17.360 --> 00:44:20.060
That's called vipashyana.

00:44:21.120 --> 00:44:32.380
And I have been studying shamatha, 
my mind is peaceful. I can keep that thought 
even in the difficult situation in the kitchen.

00:44:39.100 --> 00:44:44.680
By the way, did we do a vipashyana? 
We did a shamatha meditation 
when we did the eight levels.

00:44:48.960 --> 00:44:51.640
Did we do a vipashyana meditation?

00:44:52.440 --> 00:44:55.960
Yeah, we did. We did two.

00:44:56.540 --> 00:45:04.520
One was called dependent origination, meaning 
"in my past life, what did I do to see my lama like this?"

00:45:11.220 --> 00:45:13.700
That was a dependent origination meditation.

00:45:14.920 --> 00:45:17.680
Then we also did an emptiness meditation.

00:45:18.000 --> 00:45:27.340
We tried to imagine a lama who appeared 
at my house because they drove in a car 
from their house to my house.

00:45:32.480 --> 00:45:36.340
That's the same as an "I didn't do anything husband."

00:45:39.540 --> 00:45:43.660
That lama doesn't exist. That husband doesn't exist.

00:45:45.700 --> 00:45:50.040
The lama is coming from you. 
The husband is coming from you.

00:45:50.280 --> 00:45:56.740
So we're trying shamatha, which is to be able to keep our mind even in the difficult kitchen,

00:45:57.240 --> 00:46:02.480
many things going on, but I have focus 
so I can keep my mind on an idea.

00:46:10.560 --> 00:46:12.360
What idea?

00:46:12.700 --> 00:46:14.480
vipashyana.

00:46:15.180 --> 00:46:18.220
He comes from me, he doesn't come from his own side.

00:46:19.080 --> 00:46:24.300
"He comes from me because I yelled at my kids."
That's dependent origination.

00:46:27.120 --> 00:46:31.040
He's not just coming from his own side for no reason.

00:46:32.020 --> 00:46:33.849
That's emptiness.

00:46:33.849 --> 00:46:38.500
Now, to keep that shamatha 
and to keep those two parts of vipashyana,

00:46:42.500 --> 00:46:48.980
you need to, all day long, be nice to other people.

00:46:50.700 --> 00:46:54.760
And if you're not nice to other people all day long,

00:46:56.380 --> 00:46:59.400
You will not be able to reach shamatha.

00:47:02.100 --> 00:47:07.360
And that was the big breakthrough 
that Tsongkapa taught.

00:47:10.900 --> 00:47:13.660
If you're not nice to people all day long,

00:47:15.740 --> 00:47:19.100
you can forget trying to meditate.

00:47:21.240 --> 00:47:29.340
Why? 
Because what you hear inside your mind 
is also coming from seeds in your mind.

00:47:32.900 --> 00:47:36.160
If you're not nice to other people

00:47:37.280 --> 00:47:39.540
all day long,

00:47:40.200 --> 00:47:43.360
and you do mean things to other people,

00:47:44.580 --> 00:47:47.880
then when you sit down to meditate,

00:47:48.700 --> 00:47:53.100
those 'mean things' seeds are going to open in your mind.

00:47:56.060 --> 00:47:58.660
And they will disturb your meditation.

00:47:59.380 --> 00:48:06.240
No person who hurts other people can meditate. 
Period. 
Not possible.

00:48:09.440 --> 00:48:12.400
Therefore they cannot have shamatha.

00:48:13.040 --> 00:48:16.300
Therefore they cannot have vipashyana.

00:48:16.740 --> 00:48:23.000
And therefore they are stuck 
in the prison of the Wheel of Life.

00:48:25.120 --> 00:48:29.340
Okay, see you in session 24.

00:48:29.360 --> 00:48:33.560
Thank you Stanley for such a great translation.

